    "storyline": {
      "real": "Hill takes pole, but Berger and Alesi pass him at the start and the one-stopping Benettons hold him up. Williams bring him in on lap 20 for a short stop and a small fuel load, and he leads once the Benettons have stopped. After his second stop on lap 34 he comes out just behind Berger and cannot find a way past. Berger's engine fails in the closing laps, and Hill wins by 11.5 s from Alesi."
    },
