      "label": "Win on two stops, as Hill did"
    },
    "hardCalls": {
      "HIL": 0,
      "BER": 0
    },
    "briefing": "Hockenheim, 1996. Hill took pole but lost two places at the start, and after 17 laps you run him third, close behind Berger and Alesi in the two Benettons. Williams have Hill on two stops; the Benettons will stop once. Get him into clear air and win."
  },
